    <div class="wb-head">
      <div class="wb-head-main">
        <h1>Tools for AI agents <span class="wb-chip">MCP · llms.txt · URL</span></h1>
        <p class="wb-about">Point your terminal AI at Penumbra Forge and give it {{ (tools | length) }} privacy-first dev &amp; security tools. Three ways in — a native <strong>MCP server</strong>, a machine index at <strong>/llms.txt</strong>, or invoke any tool <strong>by URL</strong> and read a structured result. Everything runs client-side or on your own machine; nothing is uploaded.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="wb-agents">
      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">01</div>
        <h2>Connect via MCP</h2>
        <p>The native way. Add Penumbra Forge as a Model Context Protocol server and your agent (Claude Code, Cursor, Claude Desktop, any MCP client) gets every deterministic tool as a callable function — hash, HMAC, base64/hex/url, JWT decode, UUID, entropy, CIDR, and more.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">local — runs on your machine <span class="wb-badge wb-badge--local">private</span></div>
          <pre data-copy><span class="hl-dim"># nothing leaves your machine</span>
claude mcp add penumbra -- node ./workers/mcp/local.mjs</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">remote — hosted edge worker <span class="wb-badge wb-badge--local">live</span></div>
          <pre data-copy>claude mcp add --transport http penumbra https://penumbra-mcp.penumbraforge.workers.dev</pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">02</div>
        <h2>Discover via llms.txt</h2>
        <p>Tell your agent to read <a href="/llms.txt"><code>penumbraforge.com/llms.txt</code></a> — a machine-readable catalog of every tool, its purpose, and its invoke pattern. The full JSON index is at <a href="/tools/index.json"><code>/tools/index.json</code></a>.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">agent prompt</div>
          <pre data-copy>Read https://penumbraforge.com/llms.txt and use the tools there.</pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">03</div>
        <h2>Invoke any tool by URL</h2>
        <p>Every tool page takes input from the URL, runs client-side, and publishes a machine-readable result — a browser-using agent just navigates and reads it. Same links are shareable for humans.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">GET a tool</div>
          <pre data-copy>GET https://penumbraforge.com/tools/hash-generator/?in=hello&amp;algo=SHA-256</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">read the result (after html[data-pf-ready="1"])</div>
          <pre>document.querySelector('#pf-result').textContent   <span class="hl-dim">// JSON</span>
window.PF_RESULT   <span class="hl-dim">// { tool, ok, output, data }</span></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-related">
      <div class="wb-related-label">Tools available to agents right now (via MCP)</div>
      <div class="wb-mcp-grid" id="mcpGrid"></div>
